  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ヒメマツバボタン」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%92%E3%83%A1%E3%83%9E%E3%83%84%E3%83%90%E3%83%9C%E3%82%BF%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107603930,
      "text": "ヒメマツバボタン はスベリヒユ科の多肉質一年草または多年草。別名：ケツメクサ、ケヅメグサ（毛爪草）。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Portulaca pilosa」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portulaca_pilosa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1371794767,
      "text": "Portulaca pilosa is a species of flowering succulent plant in the purslane family, Portulacaceae, which is native to the Americas. Its common names include pink purslane, kiss-me-quick, and hairy pigweed. Its range extends from the southern United States and the Caribbean to as far south as Brazil.\nIt is a succulent plant with linear leaves and pink flowers."
    }
